# Development Guidelines

## Code Style and Formatting

The project uses ESLint and Prettier for code formatting and style enforcement:
- [.eslintrc](mdc:.eslintrc) - ESLint configuration
- [.prettierrc](mdc:.prettierrc) - Prettier configuration

## TypeScript Usage

- All new code should be written in TypeScript
- Types and interfaces should be placed in [src/interfaces](mdc:src/interfaces)
- Use TypeScript's strict mode as configured in [tsconfig.json](mdc:tsconfig.json)

## Component Structure

1. React components should be placed in [src/components](mdc:src/components)
2. Each component should:
   - Have its own directory
   - Include an index.ts file for exports
   - Include TypeScript interfaces for props
   - Follow the component configuration in [components.json](mdc:components.json)

## State Management

- Use React Context for global state ([src/contexts](mdc:src/contexts))
- Custom hooks should be placed in [src/hooks](mdc:src/hooks)
- Keep component state local when possible

## API and Data Handling

- HTTP requests should be organized in [src/http](mdc:src/http)
- Data persistence utilities in [src/storage](mdc:src/storage)
- Use proper error handling and loading states

## Monitoring and Debugging

Application monitoring is configured through:
- [sentry.edge.config.ts](mdc:sentry.edge.config.ts)
- [sentry.server.config.ts](mdc:sentry.server.config.ts)
- [src/instrumentation.ts](mdc:src/instrumentation.ts)
